<title>USA: U.S. Stockpile to announce sales plan Nov 6.</title>
<headline>U.S. Stockpile to announce sales plan Nov 6.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense National Stockpile Center said Thursday its plans for sales of additional commodities including cobalt and natural rubber in fiscal 1997 would be formalized Nov 6.</p>
<p>The additional sales authority was signed into law by President Clinton Sept 23 as part of the Defense authorization bill, and the Stockpile must wait 45 days to give Congress time to raise last-minute objections, a Stockpile spokesman said.</p>
<p>The additional materials the Stockpile aims to sell in fiscal 1997, which began Tuesday, are:</p>
<p>    Cobalt		     6,000,000 lbs contained</p>
<p>    Ferrocolumbium		60,000 lbs contained</p>
<p>    Germanium			4,000 kg</p>
<p>    Indium			  35,000 troy oz</p>
<p>    Palladium		     15,000 troy oz</p>
<p>    Platinum			10,000 troy oz</p>
<p>    Rubber, natural	     60,000 long tons</p>
<p>    Tantalum carbide	     2,000 lbs contained</p>
<p>    Tantalum mineral, powder 100,000 lbs contained</p>
<p>    Tantalum oxide		20,000 lbs contained</p>
<p>These materials will be added to the agency's annual sales plan for fiscal 1997.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk 202-898-8489</p>
